<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <title>What is Module & How to Create One</title>
    <style>
        body {
            font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
            background-color: #f4f7fb;
            margin: 0;
            padding: 20px;
        }
        h1 {
            text-align: center;
            color: #2c3e50;
        }
        h2 {
            color: #34495e;
            margin-top: 25px;
        }
        .section {
            background: #ffffff;
            padding: 15px;
            margin: 15px 0;
            border-left: 6px solid #16a085;
            box-shadow: 0 4px 8px rgba(0,0,0,0.1);
        }
        code {
            background: #eee;
            padding: 8px;
            display: block;
            margin-top: 10px;
            white-space: pre-wrap;
        }
        ul, ol {
            margin-top: 10px;
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>

    <h1>What is a Module?</h1>

    <div class="section">
        <p>A module is a reusable file that contains functions, classes, or variables that can be used in other programs.</p>
        <ul>
            <li>Organizes code</li>
            <li>Improves reusability</li>
            <li>Reduces duplication</li>
            <li>Makes maintenance easier</li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="section">
        <h2>Example: Using Built-in Module (Python)</h2>
        <code>
import math
print(math.sqrt(16))
        </code>
    </div>

    <div class="section">
        <h2>How to Create Your Own Module (Python)</h2>

        <h3>Step 1: Create File</h3>
        <code>mymodule.py</code>

        <h3>Step 2: Add Functions</h3>
        <code>
# mymodule.py

def add(a, b):
    return a + b

def subtract(a, b):
    return a - b
        </code>

        <h3>Step 3: Use the Module</h3>
        <code>
# main.py

import mymodule

print(mymodule.add(5, 3))
print(mymodule.subtract(10, 4))
        </code>
    </div>

    <div class="section">
        <h2>Different Ways to Import</h2>
        <code>
# Import full module
import mymodule

# Import specific function
from mymodule import add

# Rename module
import mymodule as mm
        </code>
    </div>

    <div class="section">
        <h2>JavaScript Module Example (Node.js)</h2>

        <h3>math.js</h3>
        <code>
function add(a, b) {
    return a + b;
}

module.exports = { add };
        </code>

        <h3>Use in Another File</h3>
        <code>
const math = require('./math');
console.log(math.add(5, 3));
        </code>
    </div>

</body>
</html>
